From 1404ab964bc8b44a7504c24d152bd284290b2c94 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cory Forsythe <cory@coryforsythe.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 20:15:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 07/24] docs(hermes): live-verify the /api/ws dispatch client
 against the real VPS

Every primitive (create/submit/status/history/steer/interrupt/close and
the dispatch convenience) round-tripped for real against the captain's
VPS (v0.21.2, multiplex mode): a real terminal tool call ran and
completed, session.status's literal Agent Running: Yes/No line matched
the prior scout's prediction, and session.interrupt/session.steer
returned real structural results, unlike the pane-based adapter's
key-based non-interrupt.

One real finding that updates the earlier scout report: session.create's
cwd param is not honored on this deployment (confirmed via the terminal
tool's own pwd/cat output), unlike the local scratch instance the scout
tested on an older version. Recorded as a load-bearing caveat for the
still-deferred fleet-dispatch wiring task, not re-diagnosed here.
---
 .../references/harness/hermes.md              |  8 ++--
 docs/verification/hermes.md                   | 45 ++++++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 43 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

